# Apple `container` (this Mac)

Native OCI Linux containers via Apple’s CLI (`apple/container`), **not** Docker Desktop.

- Binary: `/opt/homebrew/bin/container` (Homebrew formula, ~1.2.2)
- Data/kernels: `~/Library/Application Support/com.apple.container/`
- Prefer **Nix/mise** for non-Linux isolation; use `container` only for Linux/OCI

## On-demand (do not auto-start)

Never `brew services start container` — keeps idle RAM free.

```bash
container system start --enable-kernel-install
container run --rm --cpus 1 --memory 256M IMAGE CMD
container system stop
```

`--enable-kernel-install` avoids the interactive Kata kernel prompt (non-TTY fails with “failed to read user input”).

If no default kernel: `container system kernel set --recommended`

## Resource caps

Defaults are ~1G RAM / 4 CPUs per container. Apple does **not** reject oversubscription. For small jobs always pass `--cpus` and `--memory` (e.g. `1` and `256M`). Stop the builder when idle: `container builder stop`.

## Docker

Quit Docker Desktop while using `container`. Do not run both engines at once. Docker may stay installed for rare API-only tools.
